// The buffer model: the planned slack of a healthy seat set and how much time each exception takes from it. A hold, a replacement still to be picked, a tugger fault, a load moved off a faulted tugger and a pulled-forward seat set whose new pick order Supplier A has not yet confirmed each reduce a vehicle's buffer. The unconfirmed pick order costs resequenceSec at once and resequenceGrowthPerSec more for every real second it stays unconfirmed, so with these numbers the board reaches Watch about two minutes after the change. Tune the numbers here; getSequenceBoard reads them.
package com.vantiqse.imo

STATELESS PROCEDURE Board.bufferModel(): Object

var model = {plannedSlackSec: 860, watchSec: 660, holdSec: 320, replacementPendingSec: 60, tuggerFaultSec: 330, reassignSec: 150, resequenceSec: 120, resequenceGrowthPerSec: 0.7}
return model
